{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_015eETQT3uZuPp4k8vE7W2V4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Summary: `anchor_gui.py`\n\n**Goal / role.** `anchor_gui.py` is the Anchor productivity system's primary application: a self-contained Python-stdlib HTTP server that serves an interactive dashboard and exposes API endpoints so every UI action (done/add/capture/edit) writes directly to the markdown source files, logs the change, and refreshes state (module docstring, lines 1â€“14).\n\nGrounded bullet claims (each verified against the file):\n\n- **Stdlib-only HTTP server.** Imports are stdlib (`json, logging, os, re, socket, sys, threading, time, traceback, webbrowser`, `http.server`, `urllib.parse`, `html`) plus the local `paths` helper â€” no third-party imports in this module (lines 16â€“27).\n- **Path/data-dir resolution is delegated to `paths`.** All file constants (`DASHBOARD_MD`, `PROJECTS_MD`, `INBOX_MD`, `DOMAINS_DIR`, `LOGS_DIR`, `CANCELLED_MD`, `SAVED_FOR_LATER_MD`) resolve through `_paths`, honoring `ANCHOR_DATA_DIR`; `ANCHOR_DIR` is the code dir for static assets (lines 27â€“47).\n- **Process-wide write lock.** A shared `WRITE_LOCK` (`_paths.WRITE_LOCK`) guards every markdown/JSON mutation against concurrent `ThreadingHTTPServer` requests; the `_with_write_lock` decorator wraps mutating ops (lines 29â€“31, 3885).\n- **Cache-busting / self-healing client.** A `BUILD_ID` is computed once at startup from `git rev-parse --short HEAD` (falling back to source-file mtime); a `_CACHE_BUST_JS_TEMPLATE` client script unregisters stale service workers and clears Cache Storage on redeploy (lines 74â€“144).\n- **Markdown parsing layer.** `parse_tasks_from_md`, `parse_projects_from_md`, `parse_inbox_from_md`, `parse_archived_tasks` read markdown into dicts; `serialize_task_line` writes them back; `gather_all` aggregates DASHBOARD.md + domain files with dedup (lines 181â€“388).\n- **Task lifecycle operations.** `mark_done`, `mark_undone`, `add_task`, `capture_inbox`, `edit_task`, `edit_project`, `cancel_task`, `save_for_later`, `restore_task`, `link_task`, plus `_remove_task_from_files`/`_append_to_archive` implement the activeâ†’done/cancelled/saved/restored state machine (lines 3908â€“4318).\n- **Hand-rolled WebSocket codec.** Stdlib RFC-6455 helpers â€” `ws_accept_key`, `encode_text_frame`, `encode_close_frame`, `encode_pong_frame`, `_encode_frame`, `decode_frames` â€” back the v3/v4 ConPTY terminal transport with no library dependency (lines 463â€“634).\n- **Traversal-safe static asset routes.** `_unsafe_path_seg` guards `anchor_term_asset`, `xterm_asset`, and `brand_asset` (vendored anchor-term / xterm.js / Ghost World Labs brand mark) (lines 634â€“751).\n- **R&D project surface.** Functions render the per-project cockpit: `render_project_window_html` (the largest, lines 1856â€“3646), Kanban/lane rendering (`_render_kanban_html`, `_render_lane_sessions`, `_render_grass_board`), status lights/dots, effort cards, cost/tokens/time rollups (`render_header_rollup_html`, `render_cost_rollup_html`, `_fmt_rollup_line`), deliverables (`ensure_anchor_deliverable`, `render_deliverables_html`), and summary triggers (`_trigger_project_summary`, `_trigger_session_summary`) (lines 905â€“3885).\n- **Single HTML generator.** `generate_html(projects, tasks, inbox)` builds the entire dashboard (embedded CSS + JS) as one f-string spanning ~lines 4320â€“6270.\n- **Request handler.** `AnchorHandler(BaseHTTPRequestHandler)` (lines 6270â€“7930) implements the GET `/` + GET/POST `/api/*` routes; the file contains 48 path-dispatch checks, covering the task, inbox, lifecycle, and R&D v2/v3/v4 endpoints documented in CLAUDE.md.\n- **Single-instance bind guard.** `_ExclusiveThreadingHTTPServer` and `make_server(host=\"127.0.0.1\", port=8777)` use exclusive binding (via `paths` helpers) so a duplicate Anchor process exits cleanly rather than squatting on port 8777; `resolve_bind_host` and `main()` complete the entry path; a `_heartbeat_watchdog` thread runs alongside (lines 7930â€“8093).\n\n**Findings / notes.** The file is large (8,093 lines); the bulk is HTML/JS generation (`generate_html` â‰ˆ1,950 lines and `render_project_window_html` â‰ˆ1,790 lines). Default bind is loopback `127.0.0.1:8777`. No errors observed in the read regions.\n\n**Provenance:** claims above are read directly from `anchor_gui.py` (line numbers cited). I did not verify runtime behavior â€” only the source structure."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2918,"cache_read_input_tokens":51595,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2918},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2b5cb374-2ef1-4e73-bda7-039b7c4b1bb4","uuid":"f85a2126-0040-41c9-8986-f7e26a063268","request_id":"req_011Cc1JS7pADcjDYn3eFANaT"}
